The default configuration for built-in OpenCode agents like `plan` and `build` is not stored as a visible file in your `.config/opencode` folder. Those defaults are internal to OpenCode.

OpenCode documents `build` and `plan` as built-in primary agents:
https://opencode.ai/docs/agents/

You can override them in your own config:

%USERPROFILE%\.config\opencode\opencode.jsonc

or project-specific in:

<project-root>\opencode.json

OpenCode config docs:
https://opencode.ai/docs/config/

Permissions docs:
https://opencode.ai/docs/permissions/

Example:

{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "agent": {
    "plan": {
      "mode": "primary",
      "permission": {
        "edit": "deny",
        "bash": {
          "*": "ask",
          "git status*": "allow",
          "git diff*": "allow",
          "rg *": "allow"
        }
      }
    },
    "build": {
      "mode": "primary",
      "permission": {
        "edit": "ask",
        "bash": {
          "*": "ask",
          "npm test*": "allow",
          "git status*": "allow",
          "git diff*": "allow"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

